{"data": [{"author_id": "17217640", "created_at": "2026-11-05T20:38:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118442729390645747"], "id": "2118442729390645747", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 3, "impression_count": 2154, "like_count": 59, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 13}, "text": "In an announcement today, @blueorigin unveils a new third stage for its New Glenn rockets as well as a new first-stage engine, which is called \"Northstar.\" https://t.co/Jj6o71bolS", "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 37, "id": "235348644", "start": 26, "username": "blueorigin"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/Jj6o71bolS", "end": 179, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/SpaceflightNow/status/2118442729390645747/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2118442461714374656", "start": 156, "url": "https://t.co/Jj6o71bolS"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/Jj6o71bolS", "end": 179, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/SpaceflightNow/status/2118442729390645747/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2118442498297044992", "start": 156, "url": "https://t.co/Jj6o71bolS"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/Jj6o71bolS", "end": 179, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/SpaceflightNow/status/2118442729390645747/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2118442536381333505", "start": 156, "url": "https://t.co/Jj6o71bolS"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/Jj6o71bolS", "end": 179, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/SpaceflightNow/status/2118442729390645747/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2118442560817332224", "start": 156, "url": "https://t.co/Jj6o71bolS"}]}, "url": "https://x.com/SpaceflightNow/status/2118442729390645747"}, {"author_id": "17217640", "created_at": "2026-11-05T20:02:07.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118433698739859533"], "id": "2118433698739859533", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 3, "impression_count": 2964, "like_count": 40, "quote_count": 2, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 6}, "text": "The eighth and final ISS Roll-Out Solar Array (IROSA) has been successfully installed on the space station by @astro_anil and @Astro_Kutryk with support from their colleagues on the ISS and at @NASAJohnson. https://t.co/LXVBjhxj0u", "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 121, "id": "1456357980216066048", "start": 110, "username": "astro_anil"}, {"end": 139, "id": "798240312908910593", "start": 126, "username": "Astro_Kutryk"}, {"end": 205, "id": "50115087", "start": 193, "username": "NASAJohnson"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/LXVBjhxj0u", "end": 230, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/SpaceflightNow/status/2118433698739859533/video/1", "media_key": "13_2118433464571576321", "start": 207, "url": "https://t.co/LXVBjhxj0u"}]}, "url": "https://x.com/SpaceflightNow/status/2118433698739859533"}, {"author_id": "17217640", "created_at": "2026-11-05T19:43:24.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118428991225012513"], "id": "2118428991225012513", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2919, "like_count": 14, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 5}, "text": "The eighth and final @Redwire-built ISS Roll-Out Solar Array is now being deployed. @Astro_Kutryk and @astro_anil have been in the midst of this spacewalk since 7:36 am CT / 8:36 am ET.\n\nWatch live: https://t.co/OHkIqWhmfL https://t.co/BHFxX0GOeq", "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 29, "id": "1275427530066079744", "start": 21, "username": "Redwire"}, {"end": 97, "id": "798240312908910593", "start": 84, "username": "Astro_Kutryk"}, {"end": 113, "id": "1456357980216066048", "start": 102, "username": "astro_anil"}], "urls": [{"description": "NASA astronaut Anil Menon and Canadian Space Agency astronaut Joshu...", "display_url": "youtube.com/watch?v=iShR_6…", "end": 222, "expanded_url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=iShR_6cIuy4", "images": [{"height": 720, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2118428994773360640/xfff8s97?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1280}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2118428994773360640/xfff8s97?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 199, "status": 200, "title": "Live: Spacewalkers install improved solar array to boost space station power", "unwound_url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=iShR_6cIuy4", "url": "https://t.co/OHkIqWhmfL"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/BHFxX0GOeq", "end": 246, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/SpaceflightNow/status/2118428991225012513/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2118428968478994433", "start": 223, "url": "https://t.co/BHFxX0GOeq"}]}, "url": "https://x.com/SpaceflightNow/status/2118428991225012513"}, {"author_id": "19355829", "created_at": "2026-11-05T17:35:38.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118396837489193124"], "id": "2118396837489193124", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 3621, "like_count": 38, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 5, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "ISS spacewalk.  They meant to say EST, not EDT, I believe. https://t.co/eZ7SYRkVCP", "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/Space_Station/…", "end": 82, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/Space_Station/status/2118338906630640050", "start": 59, "url": "https://t.co/eZ7SYRkVCP"}]}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118338906630640050", "type": "quoted"}], "url": "https://x.com/planet4589/status/2118396837489193124"}, {"author_id": "17217640", "created_at": "2026-11-05T16:48:19.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118384929788883272"], "id": "2118384929788883272", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 2, "impression_count": 4507, "like_count": 53, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 10}, "text": "The IROSA has been unfolded and @csa_asc astronaut @Astro_Kutryk (EV1 w/red stripe) and @NASA astronaut @astro_anil (EV2) are making sure it's securely mounted to the bracket at the 3B mod kit.\n\nWatch live and follow our live blog for updates: https://t.co/pCb2MxbZdI https://t.co/05SFN2cYyI", "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 40, "id": "93714983", "start": 32, "username": "csa_asc"}, {"end": 64, "id": "798240312908910593", "start": 51, "username": "Astro_Kutryk"}, {"end": 93, "id": "11348282", "start": 88, "username": "NASA"}, {"end": 115, "id": "1456357980216066048", "start": 104, "username": "astro_anil"}], "urls": [{"description": "The best source for space news: launch coverage, mission reports and the launch schedule.", "display_url": "spaceflightnow.com/live/", "end": 267, "expanded_url": "https://spaceflightnow.com/live/", "images": [{"height": 683, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2118342234273701888/yumx_pxh?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1024}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2118342234273701888/yumx_pxh?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 244, "status": 200, "title": "SFN Live — Spaceflight Now", "unwound_url": "https://spaceflightnow.com/live/", "url": "https://t.co/pCb2MxbZdI"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/05SFN2cYyI", "end": 291, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/SpaceflightNow/status/2118384929788883272/video/1", "media_key": "13_2118384654772219904", "start": 268, "url": "https://t.co/05SFN2cYyI"}]}, "url": "https://x.com/SpaceflightNow/status/2118384929788883272"}, {"author_id": "21436960", "created_at": "2026-11-05T16:14:21.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118376382463889894"], "id": "2118376382463889894", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 24, "impression_count": 21201, "like_count": 396, "quote_count": 12, "reply_count": 22, "retweet_count": 81}, "text": "Closing in on Didymos. ☄️\n\nOur planetary defence mission Hera has captured its first close-up of the binary asteroid system, 60 km away, as it prepares to investigate the aftermath of DART’s historic impact with Dimorphos.\n\nDetailed images of both asteroids are coming on 25 https://t.co/VJmlvAtNwi", "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/VJmlvAtNwi", "end": 298, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/esa/status/2118376382463889894/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2118375862630219776", "start": 275, "url": "https://t.co/VJmlvAtNwi"}]}, "url": "https://x.com/esa/status/2118376382463889894"}, {"author_id": "16319797", "created_at": "2026-11-05T15:20:38.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118362862334714313"], "id": "2118362862334714313", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 5, "impression_count": 1628, "like_count": 25, "quote_count": 2, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 9}, "text": "The @QuantumSciCtr at @ORNL, @IBM, and @AMD deploy a new co-design platform for quantum error correction at IBM’s site in Poughkeepsie, New York. \n\nThe platform enables low-latency quantum-classical workflows for advancing quantum computing research: https://t.co/tCI0WKswba https://t.co/Y6TLM4MnRi", "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 18, "id": "1304221943458037760", "start": 4, "username": "QuantumSciCtr"}, {"end": 27, "id": "16145097", "start": 22, "username": "ORNL"}, {"end": 33, "id": "18994444", "start": 29, "username": "IBM"}, {"end": 43, "id": "14861876", "start": 39, "username": "AMD"}], "urls": [{"description": "The U.S. DOE’s Quantum Science Center at Oak Ridge National Lab is leading the integration of IBM quantum hardware with ORNL HPC clusters, powered by AMD.", "display_url": "ibm.co/6012EV4lM", "end": 274, "expanded_url": "https://ibm.co/6012EV4lM", "images": [{"height": 2160, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2118349207094386688/8FL4sbys?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 3840}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2118349207094386688/8FL4sbys?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 251, "status": 200, "title": "ORNL, IBM, AMD launch co-design platform for QEC | IBM Quantum Computing Blog", "unwound_url": "https://www.ibm.com/quantum/blog/ornl-amd-error-correction-co-design-platform", "url": "https://t.co/tCI0WKswba"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/Y6TLM4MnRi", "end": 298, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/IBMResearch/status/2118362862334714313/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2118362856030683136", "start": 275, "url": "https://t.co/Y6TLM4MnRi"}]}, "url": "https://x.com/IBMResearch/status/2118362862334714313"}, {"author_id": "17217640", "created_at": "2026-11-05T13:58:29.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118342190921376162"], "id": "2118342190921376162", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 4, "impression_count": 5075, "like_count": 57, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 3, "retweet_count": 15}, "text": "Happening now: NASA astronaut @astro_anil and Canadian Space Agency astronaut @Astro_Kutryk are performing a spacewalk to install the final ISS Roll-Out Solar Array.\n\nWatch live and follow updates on our live blog: https://t.co/pCb2Mxbroa https://t.co/0b9FDHFwxl", "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 41, "id": "1456357980216066048", "start": 30, "username": "astro_anil"}, {"end": 91, "id": "798240312908910593", "start": 78, "username": "Astro_Kutryk"}], "urls": [{"description": "The best source for space news: launch coverage, mission reports and the launch schedule.", "display_url": "spaceflightnow.com/live/", "end": 238, "expanded_url": "https://spaceflightnow.com/live/", "images": [{"height": 683, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2118342234273701888/yumx_pxh?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1024}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2118342234273701888/yumx_pxh?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 215, "status": 200, "title": "SFN Live — Spaceflight Now", "unwound_url": "https://spaceflightnow.com/live/", "url": "https://t.co/pCb2Mxbroa"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/0b9FDHFwxl", "end": 262, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/SpaceflightNow/status/2118342190921376162/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2118342147967434752", "start": 239, "url": "https://t.co/0b9FDHFwxl"}]}, "url": "https://x.com/SpaceflightNow/status/2118342190921376162"}, {"author_id": "11348282", "created_at": "2026-11-05T12:00:44.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118312556548784475"], "id": "2118312556548784475", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 152, "impression_count": 848990, "like_count": 2485, "quote_count": 53, "reply_count": 173, "retweet_count": 468}, "text": "LIVE: Watch as @astro_anil and Joshua Kutryk of @csa_asc install the final roll-out solar array on the @space_station during a spacewalk that will last about seven hours. The solar arrays will boost power to the orbital lab. https://t.co/wAkkOdTJQR", "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 26, "id": "1456357980216066048", "start": 15, "username": "astro_anil"}, {"end": 56, "id": "93714983", "start": 48, "username": "csa_asc"}, {"end": 117, "id": "1451773004", "start": 103, "username": "Space_Station"}], "urls": [{"description": "U.S. Spacewalk 101", "display_url": "x.com/i/broadcasts/2…", "end": 248, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/i/broadcasts/2qVjWBPJdyoyEN", "images": [{"height": 2160, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2118312443847819264/Pazn4mHV?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 3840}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2118312443847819264/Pazn4mHV?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 225, "status": 200, "title": "NASA", "unwound_url": "https://x.com/i/broadcasts/2qVjWBPJdyoyEN", "url": "https://t.co/wAkkOdTJQR"}]}, "url": "https://x.com/NASA/status/2118312556548784475"}, {"author_id": "21436960", "created_at": "2026-11-05T08:44:23.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118263144996905025"], "id": "2118263144996905025", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 63, "impression_count": 33669, "like_count": 691, "quote_count": 26, "reply_count": 27, "retweet_count": 132}, "text": "Mars may not be geologically dead after all. 🔴\n\nOur ExoMars Trace Gas Orbiter has detected hydrogen chloride above volcanic fissures in the Alba Mons region, which scientists suggest could be linked to dormant volcanic activity beneath the surface.\n\nRead more: https://t.co/7D4B8MggQi", "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/7D4B8MggQi", "end": 284, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/esa/status/2118263144996905025/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2118262641541910528", "start": 261, "url": "https://t.co/7D4B8MggQi"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/7D4B8MggQi", "end": 284, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/esa/status/2118263144996905025/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2118262640510185472", "start": 261, "url": "https://t.co/7D4B8MggQi"}]}, "url": "https://x.com/esa/status/2118263144996905025"}, {"author_id": "46648807", "created_at": "2026-11-04T22:45:09.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118112340549771487"], "id": "2118112340549771487", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1241, "like_count": 6, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "When investigators are working to solve a criminal case, they sometimes call upon experts who identify faces, and the experts rely on a part of the face you might not expect. \n\nLearn more in our latest Taking Measure blog post: https://t.co/BEWBt4EVSc https://t.co/hKnnDrkSas", "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "How do experts identify faces? Their methods might surprise you.", "display_url": "nist.gov/blogs/taking-m…", "end": 251, "expanded_url": "https://www.nist.gov/blogs/taking-measure/facial-recognition-experts-can-identify-you-your-ears", "start": 228, "status": 200, "title": "Facial Recognition Experts Can Identify You by … Your Ears?", "unwound_url": "https://www.nist.gov/blogs/taking-measure/facial-recognition-experts-can-identify-you-your-ears", "url": "https://t.co/BEWBt4EVSc"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/hKnnDrkSas", "end": 275, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/NIST/status/2118112340549771487/video/1", "media_key": "7_2118112310816358402", "start": 252, "url": "https://t.co/hKnnDrkSas"}]}, "url": "https://x.com/NIST/status/2118112340549771487"}, {"author_id": "626660983", "created_at": "2026-11-04T21:37:33.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118095329480634825"], "id": "2118095329480634825", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 5, "impression_count": 17064, "like_count": 634, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 21, "retweet_count": 21}, "text": "don't do it DeSantis\n\nkeep ur hands clean son https://t.co/YbHXIHIplZ", "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/JustinTLogan/s…", "end": 69, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/JustinTLogan/statu